{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790970225,"nonce":"aGU9JwihUroc/GP9vb0GAuRMU7I=","title":"A drop placed after _setjmp runs twice when an exception longjmps back","message":"Two try/catch blocks over a tracked variable with `Sys.println(\"A \" + i)` between them hit\nSIGTRAP in `_xzm_xzone_malloc_freelist_outlined` (double free) on Cranelift and LLVM.\n\nThe CLIF has the drop of the `\"A \" + i` string after `_setjmp` in the same block\n(`v22 = call setjmp; call free(v20); brif`). When a throw longjmps back to that setjmp, the free\nruns a second time. Suspect ir/insert_free.rs placing drops before the terminator of the block that\nholds `push_handler`/`_setjmp` (emitted in ir/mir/expr/exceptions.rs): nothing may be freed\nbetween the setjmp and its branch.\n\n```haxe\nclass Main { static function main() {\n  var i = 0;\n  try { throw 5; } catch (s:Int) { i = 1; } catch (e:Dynamic) { i = 2; }\n  Sys.println(\"A \" + i);\n  try { throw 6; } catch (s:Int) { i = 3; } catch (e:Dynamic) { i = 4; }\n  Sys.println(\"B \" + i); // A 1 / B 3; rayzor: SIGTRAP in malloc after \"A 1\"\n}}\n```","files":null}]}